[50.785, "\u001b[H\r\u001b[26B \u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \u001b[24G\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[3G\u001b[39mMemory bandwidth is capped near 63 GB/s, and per-load tweaks don't help. I'm next instrumenting argmax and\u001b[110Gthe\u001b[114GLOGITS\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bwrites, since matmul runs slightly slower in the\u001b[52Greal\u001b[57Gprogram\u001b[65Gthan\u001b[70Gin\u001b[73Gthe\u001b[77Gmicrobenchmark.\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m \u001b[3G\u001b[39mRunning \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command\u2026\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m\u2722\u001b[3GWanderin\u001b[38;2;245;149;117mg\u2026\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m \u001b[38;2;102;102;102m(45s \u00b7 \u2193\u001b[23G4.2k tokens \u00b7 thought for 22s)\r\u001b[1B  \u23bf \u00a0Tip: Use /btw to ask a quick\u001b[35Gside question without interrupting Claude's current work\u001b[39m\u001b[40;1H\u001b[38;3H"]
