[59.934, "\u001b[H\u001b[3G\u001b[1mRemaining limitations:\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[22m- The Mojo runtime starts\u001b[29G4\u001b[31Gworker\u001b[38Gthreads\u001b[46Gof\u001b[49Gits\u001b[53Gown\u001b[57Gwhen\u001b[62Gthe\u001b[66Gprocess\u001b[74Glaunches.\u001b[84GThey\u001b[89Gsat\u001b[93Gidle\u001b[98Gfor\u001b[102G100%\u001b[107Gof\u001b[110Gthe\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gprofile;\u001b[14GI left them alone because the rules forbid\u001b[57Gsetting th\u001b[68Gead counts.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GLoad\u001b[10Gng now briefly needs an extra\u001b[40G98 MB buffer, freed before \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mREADY\u001b[39m.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1BI only pr\u001b[15Gfiled phase by phas\u001b[35G at the\u001b[43Gshort d\u001b[51Gvelopm\u001b[58Gnt cont\u001b[66Gxts (at\u001b[74Gmost\u001b[79G82\u001b[82Gpositions).\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BNOTES.md\u001b[12Ghas\u001b[16Gthe\u001b[20Gprofiling\u001b[30Gevidence,\u001b[40Gthe\u001b[44Gchanges,\u001b[53Gthe\u001b[57Gtests\u001b[63Gand\u001b[67Gthe\u001b[71Glimitations.\u001b[84GThe\u001b[88Gprofiling\u001b[98Gtools\u001b[104Gare\u001b[108Gin\u001b[111G\u001b[38;2;87;105;247mprof/\u001b[117G\u001b[39mso\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bthe measurements\u001b[20Gcan be rep\u001b[31Gated; \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mmj.mojo\u001b[39m itself contain\u001b[60G no profiling code.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m\u273b\u001b[3GWorked for 10m 31s \u00b7 done 5:24 PM\r\u001b[1B\u001b[3"]
[59.935, "9m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;240;240;240m\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m\u276f \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mProfile this implementation on the supplied development workloads. Improve performance within the same rules and \u001b[39m     \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mrema\u001b[8Gning budget. Preserve the\u001b[34Ginterface and correctness requirements. Do not use hidden evaluation inputs, external \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bimpleme\u001b[11Gtations or oth\u001b[27G ports. Record profiling \u001b[53Gvid\u001b[57Gnce, changes, tests\u001b[77Gand\u001b[81Gremaining limitations\u001b[105G NOTES.md.\u001b[39m     \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[3G\u001b[39mStarting\u001b[12Gpoint:\u001b[19Gthe\u001b[23Gforward\u001b[31Gpass\u001b[36Gis\u001b[39G7.42\u001b[44Gms/token\u001b[53Gagainst\u001b[61Ga\u001b[63Gmeasured\u001b[72Gstreaming\u001b[82Gfloor\u001b[88Gof\u001b[91G~7.0\u001b[96Gms,\u001b[100Gso\u001b[103Gwhat's\u001b[110Gleft\u001b[115Gis\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3Gsm\u001b[6Gll. First I'll get the full end-to-end \u001b[46Gplit (forward vs\u001b[63Geverything else, such as\u001b[88Gargmax,\u001b[96GLOGITS\u001b[103Gfile writes\u001b[115Gand\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bprotocol). Then I'll check whether \u001b[39Ghe 62.5 GB/s \"ceiling\" is really fixed. One \u001b[84Gypothesis is that hardware\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Befetcher"]
