[93.169, "\u001b[H\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[39m Starting point: the forward pass is 7.42 ms/token against a measured streaming floor\u001b[88Gof\u001b[91G~7.0\u001b[96Gms,\u001b[100Gso\u001b[103Gwhat's\u001b[110Gleft\u001b[115Gis\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B small. First I'll get the full end-to-end split\u001b[51G(forward\u001b[60Gvs\u001b[63Geverything\u001b[74Gelse,\u001b[80Gsuch\u001b[85Gas\u001b[88Gargmax,\u001b[96GLOGITS\u001b[103Gfile\u001b[108Gwrites\u001b[115Gand\r\u001b[1B  protocol). Then I'll check whether the 62.5 GB/s \"ceiling\" is really fixed. One hypothesis is that hardware\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B prefetchers stop \u001b[21Gt 16 KB page b\u001b[36Gundaries, which\u001b[52Gsoftware\u001b[61Gprefetch\u001b[70Gfar\u001b[74Genough\u001b[81Gahead,\u001b[88Gor\u001b[91Gnon-temporal\u001b[104Gloads,\u001b[111Gmight\u001b[117Gget\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B around.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B \u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[39m Memory bandwidth is\u001b[23Gcapped\u001b[30Gnear 63 GB/s, and\u001b[48Gper-load\u001b[57Gtweaks\u001b[64Gdon't\u001b[70Ghelp.\u001b[76GI'm\u001b[80Gnext\u001b[85Ginstrumenting\u001b[99Gargmax\u001b[106Gand\u001b[110Gthe\u001b[114GLOGITS\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B writes,\u001b[11Gsince\u001b[17Gmatmul runs\u001b[29Gslightly\u001b"]
[93.171, "[38Gslower\u001b[45Gin\u001b[48Gthe\u001b[52Greal\u001b[57Gprogram\u001b[65Gthan\u001b[70Gin\u001b[73Gthe\u001b[77Gmicrobenchmark.\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B \u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[39m Argmax\u001b[10Gcosts\u001b[16Gabout\u001b[22G40\u001b[25G\u00b5s\u001b[28Gper\u001b[32Gtoken\u001b[38Gand\u001b[42GLOGITS\u001b[49Gwrites\u001b[56Gabout\u001b[62G60\u001b[65G\u00b5s\u001b[68Gper\u001b[72Gposition,\u001b[82Gboth\u001b[87Gsmall.\u001b[94GThe\u001b[98Greal\u001b[103Ggap\u001b[107Gis\u001b[110Gthat\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B matmuls run\u001b[15Gat ~60 GB/s i\u001b[29Gside\u001b[34Gthe prog\u001b[43Gam versus 62.7\u001b[58GGB/s in the microbenchmark, so I'm building\u001b[102Ga\u001b[104Gcopy\u001b[109Gwhose\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B forward \u001b[12Gass runs only matmuls to find what sl\u001b[50Gws the stream.\u001b[65G\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m\u23fa\u001b[39m Co\u001b[7Ga\u001b[9Ging matmul timing\u001b[27Gwith\u001b[32Gand\u001b[36Gwithout\u001b[44Gattention\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m  \u23bf  $ cd /Users/agentlab/pvc/mj; python3 -I - <<'EOF'\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[4G \u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;102;102;102ms=open('/Users/agentlab/pvc/mj/mj.mojo').read()\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B \u001b[4G  \u001b[38;2;102;102;102ma=\"\"\" if head_size == 64:\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B \u001b["]
