[320.49, "\u001b[H\u001b[3GArgmax cos\u001b[14Gs about\u001b[22G40 \u00b5s per \u001b[33Goken and\u001b[42GLOGITS writes about 60\u001b[65G\u00b5s per position, both small. The \u001b[99Geal gap is that\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bmatmuls run at ~60 GB/s inside the program versus 62.7 GB/s\u001b[63Gin\u001b[66Gthe\u001b[70Gmicrobenchmark,\u001b[86Gso\u001b[89GI'm\u001b[93Gbuilding\u001b[102Ga\u001b[104Gcopy\u001b[109Gwhose\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bforward\u001b[11Gpass\u001b[16Gruns\u001b[21Gonly\u001b[26Gmatmuls\u001b[34Gto\u001b[37Gfind\u001b[42Gwhat\u001b[47Gslows\u001b[53Gthe\u001b[57Gstream.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m shell commands \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[3G\u001b[39mSkipping attention changes no\u001b[33Ghing, so inte\u001b[47Gleaved work isn't\u001b[65Gthe cause. Next I'll ch\u001b[89Gck\u001b[92Gw\u001b[94Gether the\u001b[104Ggap is\u001b[111Gjus\u001b[115G\u001b[K\r\u001b[3C\u001b[1Best-of-N (microbenchmark) versus\u001b[37Gmean\u001b[42G(in-program)\u001b[55Gtiming:\r\u001b[2C\u001b[4BThe m\u001b[9Gcrobenchmark matmul average\u001b[37G 7.09 ms, clo\u001b[51Ge\u001b[53Gto the\u001b[60Gprogram's 7.28\u20137.43 ms, so the leftover ~4% gap isn't a clear\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Blever. I'm now timing raw write\u001b[36Gyscalls for the 460 \u00d7\u001b[58G128 KB LOGITS output at different chunk\u001b[9"]
