[325.669, "\u001b[H\u001b[3GSkipping attenti\u001b[20Gn chan\u001b[27Ges nothing, so interle\u001b[50Gved work isn't the cau\u001b[73Ge. Next I'll check\u001b[92Gwhether the gap \u001b[109Gs just\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bbest-of-N\u001b[13G(microbenchmark) versus\u001b[37Gmean (in-program) timing:\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B \u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[3G\u001b[39mThe microbenchmark matmul\u001b[29Gaverages\u001b[38G7.09\u001b[43Gms,\u001b[47Gclose\u001b[53Gto\u001b[56Gthe\u001b[60Gprogram's\u001b[70G7.28\u20137.43\u001b[80Gms,\u001b[84Gso\u001b[87Gthe\u001b[91Gleftover\u001b[100G~4%\u001b[104Ggap\u001b[108Gisn't\u001b[114Ga\u001b[116Gclear\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Blever. I'm now timing raw write syscalls\u001b[44Gfor\u001b[48Gthe\u001b[52G460\u001b[56G\u00d7\u001b[58G128\u001b[62GKB\u001b[65GLOGITS\u001b[72Goutput\u001b[79Gat\u001b[82Gdifferent\u001b[92Gchunk\u001b[98Gsizes\u001b[104Gto\u001b[107Gsee\u001b[111Gwhether\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bbatching those writes would help.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[39m Batching the writes showed no consistent gain, so LOGITS stays as it is. Next I'll vectorize argmax while keeping the\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B first-maximum\u001b[17Gtie-breaking,\u001b[31Gand\u001b[35Gs"]
