[811.927, "\u001b[H\r\u001b[6C\u001b[3Bmicrobenchmark'\u001b[23G crossover sits near 150 pos\u001b[53Gions, but it reruns the\u001b[77Gsame\u001b[82Gposit\u001b[88Gons\u001b[92Ga\u001b[94Gd so\u001b[99Gflatters the short\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcache, since the real program's\u001b[35G438\u001b[39GMB\u001b[42Gof\u001b[45Gweights\u001b[53Gevict\u001b[59Git\u001b[62Gbetween\u001b[70Gtokens.\u001b[78GI'll\u001b[83Gadd\u001b[87Gthe\u001b[91Gper-head\u001b[100Gkernel\u001b[107Gup\u001b[110Gto\u001b[113Ga\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcompile-time\u001b[16Gthreshold\u001b[26Gand\u001b[30Gconfirm\u001b[38Gthe\u001b[42Ggain\u001b[47Gunder\u001b[53Gthe\u001b[57Ginterleaved\u001b[69GA/B\u001b[73Gharness.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[3G\u001b[39mThe short-context kernel is slower in the real\u001b[50Gprogram,\u001b[59Gso\u001b[62GI'm\u001b[66Greverting\u001b[76Git,\u001b[80Gand\u001b[84GI'll\u001b[89Gvectorize\u001b[99Gargmax\u001b[106Gnext,\u001b[112Gkeeping\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bits\u001b[7Gexact\u001b[13Gsemantics\u001b[23Gand\u001b[27GNaN\u001b[31Gbehaviour.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[3G\u001b[39mThe argmax check passes, a\u001b[30Gd I'm\u001b[36Gnow confirming it matches run.c's scalar loop on tr\u001b[88Gcky\u001b[92"]
[811.928, "Ginputs\u001b[99Glike ties, NaNs,\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Binfinities and odd lengths.\r\u001b[2B \u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[3G\u001b[39mZero mismatches in 20,000 adversarial trials, so the result is the same as run.c's loop. Measuring\u001b[102Gthe\u001b[106Ggain\u001b[111Gwith\u001b[116Gthe\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Binstrumented build and the interleaved A/B:\r\u001b[2B  \u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[39m The argmax change cut the per-call cost from 40.5 to 3.6 \u00b5s, and the interleaved\u001b[84GA/B\u001b[88Gis\u001b[91Gat\u001b[94Gor\u001b[97Gslightly\u001b[106Gahead\u001b[112Gof\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B baseline, which is within noise. Next I'll check\u001b[52Gwhat\u001b[57G\u001b[38;2;87;105;247mFileHandle.write_bytes\u001b[80G\u001b[39mdoes,\u001b[86Gsince\u001b[92Gthe\u001b[96G60\u001b[99G\u00b5s\u001b[102GLOGITS\u001b[109Gwrite\u001b[115Glooks\r\u001b[1B  slow for one kernel copy.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m \u001b[39m Inspecting FileHandle\u001b[25Gwrite_bytes im\u001b[40Glemen\u001b[46Gation\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m  \u23bf  $ sed -n 555,606p /Users/Shared/pvc-kit/mojo/docs/stdli"]
