[881.908, " faster in isolation, but\u001b[88Gonly because\u001b[101Gthe test \u001b[112Guses data\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bstill in cache. In the\u001b[28Greal\u001b[33Gprogram\u001b[41Gthe\u001b[45Gweight\u001b[52Greads\u001b[58Gpush\u001b[63Git\u001b[66Gout\u001b[70Gbetween\u001b[78Gtokens,\u001b[86Gand\u001b[90Gthere\u001b[96Gwas\u001b[100Gno\u001b[103Ggain.\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mBat\u001b[9Ghing\u001b[14Gthe LOGITS\u001b[25Gfile\u001b[30Gwri\u001b[35Gs:\u001b[22m the gain wasn't consis\u001b[61Gent. Th\u001b[70G60 \u00b5s per position is the\u001b[96Gkernel's\u001b[105G\u001b[38;2;87;105;247mwrite()\u001b[113G\u001b[39mitself,\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gand avoiding it would need libc memory-mapping, which is a gray area under the\u001b[84Gstandard-library-only rule.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mChecking the new argmax:\u001b[22m it gives the same result as run.c's loop:\u001b[70Glowe\u001b[75Gt index wins t\u001b[90Ges, +0.0 and \u22120.0 count a\u001b[116G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bequal, and NaNs behave th\u001b[29G same. A randomized test of 20,000\u001b[64Gadversarial cases against a copy of ru\u001b[103G.c's \u001b[109Goop\u001b[113Gfound\u001b[119G0\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bmismatches.\u001b[15GThat\u001b[20Gtest\u001b[25Gis\u001b[28Gin\u001b[31G\u001b[38;2;87;105;247mprof/argmax_test.mojo\u001b[39m.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mMeasureme"]
[881.909, "nt caveat:\u001b[22m a load\u001b[30Gaverage\u001b[38Gof about 3\u001b[49Gfrom\u001b[55Gther process\u001b[68Gs made single\u001b[82Gruns vary\u001b[92Gby 5\u201310%. So decisions rest\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bon \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mprof/ab.py\u001b[39m, which loads all variants together and\u001b[56Galternates\u001b[67Gshort\u001b[73Gruns\u001b[78Gbetween\u001b[86Gthem.\u001b[92GThat\u001b[97Ggives\u001b[103Gabout\u001b[109G1%\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bresolution,\u001b[15Gwhich\u001b[21Gis\u001b[24Galso\u001b[29Gthe\u001b[33Gsize\u001b[38Gof\u001b[41Gthe\u001b[45Gargmax\u001b[52Ggain.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BNOTES.md has a\u001b[18Gnew \"Pr\u001b[26Gfiling round 3\" section with the \u001b[60Gvidence tables, the rej\u001b[84Gcted experiments and their numbers,\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bthe tests and the\u001b[21Grem\u001b[25Gining lim\u001b[35Gtations. The new\u001b[52Gmeasurement\u001b[64Gand\u001b[68Gtest\u001b[73Gscripts\u001b[81Gare\u001b[85Gin\u001b[88G\u001b[38;2;87;105;247mprof/\u001b[39m.\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m\u273b\u001b[3GSaut\u00e9ed for 14m 23s \u00b7 done 5:39 PM\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[3B\u276f\u00a0\r\u001b[21C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m? for shortcuts\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[40;1H\u001b[38;3H"]
